[00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.560]   Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for standing by and welcome to the Ingersoll-Rand First Quarter 2020 Earnings Conference Call.
[00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.080]   At this time, all participants are in a listen-only mode.
[00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.940]   After the speaker's presentation, there will be a question and answer session.
[00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.880]   To ask a question during the session, you will need to press star 1 on your telephone.
[00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:25.540]   We ask that you please limit yourself to one question and one follow-up.
[00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:30.020]   If you require any further assistance, please press star 0.
[00:00:30.020 --> 00:00:35.640]   I would now like to hand the conference over to your speaker today, Vic Kinney, Head of Investor Relations.
[00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.920]   Thank you. Please go ahead.
[00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.880]   Thank you and welcome to the Ingersoll-Rand 2020 First Quarter Earnings Call.
[00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:51.340]   I'm Vic Kinney, Ingersoll-Rand's Investor Relations Leader, and with me today are Vicente Renal, Chief Executive Officer, and Emily Weaver, Chief Financial Officer.
[00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:55.460]   Our earnings release, which was issued this morning, and a supplemental presentation,
[00:00:55.540 --> 00:01:02.360]   which will be referenced during the call, are both available on the Investor Relations section of our website, www.irco.com.
[00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.040]   In addition, a replay of this morning's conference call will be available later today.
[00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:12.020]   Before we get started, I would like to remind everyone that certain of the statements on this call are forward-looking in nature
[00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.900]   and are subject to the risks and uncertainties discussed in our previous SEC filings,
[00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.600]   which you should read in conjunction with the information provided on this call.
[00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.300]   For more details on these risks, please refer to our annual report on Form 10-K,
[00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:25.520]   filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission.
[00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.860]   And our current report on Form 8-K, filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on May 1, 2020,
[00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:34.560]   which are available on our website at www.irco.com.
[00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.940]   Additional disclosure regarding forward-looking statements is included on slide 2 of the presentation.
[00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.640]   In addition, in today's remarks, we will refer to certain non-GAAP financial measures.
[00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:49.160]   You can find a reconciliation of these measures to the most comparable measure calculated and presented in accordance with GAAP
[00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:54.400]   in our slide presentation and in our release, which are both available on the Investor Relations section of our website.
[00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:54.500]   Thank you.
[00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:58.620]   I'd also remind everyone that in both our earnings release and today's presentation,
[00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:05.040]   we have included both as-reported financials and supplemental financial information to assist with analysis and comparatives.
[00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:09.440]   The as-reported financials only include the Ingersoll Rand Industrial segment results
[00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.620]   from the closing date of the transaction on February 29, 2020,
[00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:18.660]   and the supplemental financial information provides results as if the transaction had occurred as of January 1, 2018,
[00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.080]   to provide a full quarter of comparable results.
[00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:25.440]   Turning to slide 3, on today's call, we will provide an update on the topography,
[00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.300]   the top priorities of the company in the current operating environment,
[00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.720]   as well as review our first quarter total company and segment highlights.
[00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.520]   We will conclude today's call with a Q&A session.
[00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.920]   As a reminder, we would ask that each caller keep to one question and one follow-up to allow for enough time for other participants.
[00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.900]   At this time, I will now turn it over to Vicente Reynaud, Chief Executive Officer.
[00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.660]   Vicente Reynaud: Thanks, Vic, and good morning to everyone on the call.
[00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:54.600]   I would like to kick off today's presentation by sending our thoughts to all who have been affected by COVID-19
[00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.240]   and all the dedicated healthcare workers,
[00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:02.040]   first responders, and volunteers who are on the front lines all over the world battling this pandemic.
[00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:08.280]   I would also like to take a moment to say a sincere thank you to all of the Ingersoll Rand employees around the world.
[00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.800]   The pictures on slide 4 are just a few examples of our dedicated global workforce
[00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:19.460]   who have adapted to the new realities of the work environment to continue to serve our customers.
[00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.500]   Every day, I hear of new examples of our businesses providing mission-critical products to our customers.
[00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:30.700]   And I am proud of what our company represents and how our employees have responded to these unprecedented times.
[00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:41.720]   While there continues to be a lot of uncertainty about the future, one thing I am sure about is that Ingersoll Rand will continue to keep the safety of our communities and serving our customers at the center of everything we do.
[00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:46.640]   And that wouldn't be possible without the dedication and hard work of all of our employees.
[00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:53.240]   Moving to slide 5, I would like to grant everyone on the critical priorities we are following during these challenging times.
[00:03:53.240 --> 00:04:01.640]   When we closed the transaction a little over two months ago, we could have never anticipated that within a matter of weeks we would be dealing with a global pandemic
[00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:06.040]   causing disruptions to our customers' supply chain and the day-to-day operations of the company.
[00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:17.640]   Our response speaks to how the IRX toolkit has effectively helped us to plan, accelerate, and adapt our actions to act quickly and decisively around three core priorities.
[00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:21.640]   First, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.120]   Second, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:22.620]   Second, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.120]   Second, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:23.120]   Second, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:23.120]   Second, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:23.120]   Second, ensuring the safety of our employees, customers, and the community.
[00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:30.120]   Third, keeping a strong focus on the integration and execution to ensure the financial stability of the company through this uncertain time.
[00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:38.120]   And finally, continuing to execute on the strategy of the company, as we have multiple catalysts to drive ongoing value creation.
[00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:47.120]   The strength of Ingersoll Rand Team aligned around these three priorities will position the company to emerge from this crisis as a stronger and more unified company.
